WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:07.170
6. We're animals too, after all.

2
00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:16.530
Animals symbolize many different things. In Proverbs, they can represent people, our characteristics, or other elements of our lives.

3
00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:22.650
Don't count your chickens before they're hatched. Use as chicks to represent opportunities.

4
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:27.170
It reminds us not to be too sure of something that we don't have yet.

5
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:34.050
The hen may have laid ten eggs, but until they hatch, she doesn't know how many chicks there are.

6
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:41.250
A bird in hand is worth two in the bush means that what we have is more valuable than what we desire.

7
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:48.050
It tells people who always want more out of life to be satisfied with what is already theirs.

8
00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:58.130
On the other hand, the early bird catches the worm. This proverb warns us that good things will pass us by if we're too lazy to go after them.

9
00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:09.090
Sometimes, however, we just have to give up on people. A leopard can't change his spots means that although a person's behavior may change, his character won't.

10
00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:12.050
We all know someone like that, don't we?

11
00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:17.570
Sayings about animals can also include people or compare us with other creatures.

12
00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:24.850
If you hear it from the horse's mouth, you get information from someone directly involved in a situation.

13
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:32.290
To have a tiger by the tail means you have done something bad to someone who can do something worse to you.

14
00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:39.730
And if you are drawn like a moth to a flame, you're hopelessly attracted to something or someone dangerous.

15
00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:43.730
Anyone who's fallen in love should appreciate that.

16
00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:49.250
By using animals, proverbs can teach us lessons in a subtle, indirect way.

17
00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:54.530
Animal proverbs also remind us that people are part of the natural world.

18
00:01:54.530 --> 00:02:01.730
We may think we're special, but these sayings show us that we often behave in the same ways as other beings.
